<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish April industrial output fell 3.7 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Irish April industrial output fell 3.7 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish industrial production fell a seasonally  adjusted 3.7 percent in April after a 10.8 percent increase in March,  Central Statistics Office (CSO) data showed.</p>
<p>The CSO said the April unadjusted index for all industries was 278.3,  a 14.9 percent rise over April 1996.</p>
<p>-- Dublin newsroom + 353 1 676 9775</p>
